# Constants for this machine - copy to .env if you need any. Nothing here is required.
#
# Your settings (name, voice, decisions, models, agents, projects) are NOT kept here: they live in
# ~/.nova/settings.json. Change them in Settings (click ⚙ in the dock, or say "open settings")
# or edit that file by hand - Nova applies either right away. Changes to this file need a restart.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: Jev, TypeSafe's System One model, when you choose it in Settings -> Decisions (Reflex decides otherwise,
# on this Mac). Nova sends it only to api.typesafe.ai. Create one with TypeSafe; `npm run jev:ping` checks it.
NOVA_JEV_API_KEY=
# A local model server started with an API key: NOVA_<SERVER>_API_KEY (the server's name in Settings)
# NOVA_OMLX_API_KEY=

# --- Signing -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nova signs its apps with your Apple certificate when you have one (Xcode -> Settings -> Accounts makes a free
# one), so macOS keeps their permissions across rebuilds. Name another here, or "-" to sign for this Mac alone.
# NOVA_SIGN_IDENTITY="Apple Development: you@example.com (ABCDE12345)"

# --- Daemon ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port the UI connects to (ws://127.0.0.1:<port>). If you change it, set VITE_NOVA_URL in apps/desktop/.env to match.
# NOVA_PORT=7878
# Port of the door for paired iPhones, on every network this Mac is on - open only while Settings → iPhone lets them connect.
# NOVA_PHONE_PORT=7879
# Pages allowed to change settings: Nova's own windows.
# NOVA_UI_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173,tauri://localhost,http://tauri.localhost,https://tauri.localhost
# Where your settings live, an optional file of extra agent definitions (relative paths start at this folder),
# and downloaded models (Reflex's decision model).
# NOVA_SETTINGS_FILE=~/.nova/settings.json
# NOVA_AGENTS_FILE=nova.agents.json
# NOVA_MODELS_DIR=~/.nova/models
# 1 = pretend to open and quit apps (logs instead), for trying Nova out safely
# NOVA_DRY_RUN=1
